<task id="001" project="smart-todo-r5">
  <metadata>
    <title>Absorb PR #508 boundary fix on Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components (FR-01 prerequisite)</title>
    <phase>1: Shared-lib foundation</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies TypeScript source + package/tsconfig files in a shared peer package consumed by multiple hosts (LegalWorkspace, future SpaarkeAi); FR-01 prerequisite that FR-02..FR-15 downstream card/hoist work depends on. Tags include shared-lib.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>High-blast-radius: the `@spaarke/ui-components` package-boundary fix underlies every future hoist/consumer of `Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components`; getting the tsconfig `paths` / package.json dependency wiring wrong silently reintroduces the exact boundary violation PR #508 was meant to fix, breaking type-checking for all downstream consumers.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>P</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Shares `Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components` package files with the hoist spine (tasks 002/003) — those tasks add/move files into the same package immediately after this one lands; running 001 concurrently with anything else touching this package risks merge conflicts on package.json/tsconfig.json.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>react, typescript, shared-lib</tags>
    <estimated-effort>0.5-1 day</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Re-apply the stale, abandoned PR #508 (`fix/events-smarttodo-components-package-boundary`, CONFLICTING, 2026-06-29) package-boundary fix on CURRENT master for `Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components`. Rewrite the 4 relative-path imports that reach into `../../../Spaarke.UI.Components/src/...` (a private-source bypass of the `@spaarke/ui-components` package boundary) to proper `@spaarke/ui-components/...` package specifiers, in exactly these 3 files: `src/client/shared/Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/types/kanban.ts` (1 import), `src/client/shared/Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/widgets/SmartTodoWidget/SmartTodoWidget.tsx` (2 imports), `src/client/shared/Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/components/SmartTodoKanban/SmartTodoKanban.tsx` (1 import). Add `@spaarke/ui-components` as both a `dependency` (`file:../Spaarke.UI.Components`) and `peerDependency` in `Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/package.json`, and add `baseUrl` + `paths` mapping `@spaarke/ui-components` / `@spaarke/ui-components/*` to `Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/tsconfig.json` — copy the EXACT pattern already in `src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/tsconfig.json` and `package.json` (verified working reference; also consistent with `Spaarke.AI.Widgets/tsconfig.json`). Runtime semantics MUST NOT change — this is an import-path + build-config fix only.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in TypeScript project-reference boundaries, npm workspace package specifiers, and the `@spaarke/*` peer-package convention used across `src/client/shared/`. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>`Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components` type-checks (`tsc --noEmit` / `npm run build`) without surfacing any `Spaarke.UI.Components` private-source compiler errors; zero remaining `../../../Spaarke.UI.Components/src/` or `../../../../Spaarke.UI.Components/src/` import specifiers anywhere in `Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/`; `package.json` carries the `@spaarke/ui-components` dependency + peerDependency; `tsconfig.json` carries the `@spaarke/ui-components` path mapping; no runtime/behavioral change.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-01 (Prerequisite) and CLAUDE.md "PR #508 recipe" note: PR #508 proposed this exact fix but went stale/CONFLICTING and was abandoned 2026-06-29. Owner clarification (spec.md Owner Clarifications table, "PR #508 vs R5") confirmed: fold into FR-01, do not revive #508 separately; FR-01 re-applies the fix on current master, then #508 is closed as superseded at project wrap-up (task 090). This task is the FIRST step of FR-01 and MUST land before task 002 (the 13-file Kanban hoist) — the hoist will itself add imports from `@spaarke/ui-components` and must use the restored clean boundary, never the relative bypass this task removes.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/types/kanban.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/widgets/SmartTodoWidget/SmartTodoWidget.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/components/SmartTodoKanban/SmartTodoKanban.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/package.json</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/tsconfig.json</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/tsconfig.json</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components/package.json</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.AI.Widgets/tsconfig.json</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="none" status="complete">No upstream task dependency — this is the first task of the project.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">Scope: all cross-package imports in `Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components` MUST consume `@spaarke/ui-components` via its package specifier (or a documented `paths` alias resolving to its `dist/` types) — never reach into its `src/` directly. This is the boundary PR #508 restores.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: runtime behavior of `Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components` is UNCHANGED by this task — only import specifiers and build configuration (package.json, tsconfig.json) are touched. Do not alter component logic, props, or exports.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: use the `Spaarke.DailyBriefing.Components` tsconfig/package.json pattern verbatim (paths mapped to `../Spaarke.UI.Components/dist/index.d.ts` and `../Spaarke.UI.Components/dist/*`; dependency as `file:../Spaarke.UI.Components`) — do not invent a different resolution strategy.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>shared-lib package boundaries</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-012-shared-components.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-design-system.md</file>
      <file>projects/smart-todo-r5/spec.md</file>
