  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the rewritten imports, when `npm run build` (or `tsc --noEmit`) runs in `Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components`, then it succeeds WITHOUT surfacing any `Spaarke.UI.Components` private-source compiler errors.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a repo-wide grep for `Spaarke.UI.Components/src` scoped to `Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/`, when run after this task, then zero matches remain.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given `package.json`, when inspected, then it contains `@spaarke/ui-components` under both `dependencies` and `peerDependencies`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given `tsconfig.json`, when inspected, then it contains a `paths` entry mapping `@spaarke/ui-components` and `@spaarke/ui-components/*`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no component prop, export signature, or rendered output changes — a diff of `Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/src/**/*.{ts,tsx}` shows only import-statement line changes plus the two config files.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All existing unit tests in `Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components/__tests__/` pass unchanged; build is green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec section: FR-01 (Prerequisite). This is step 1 of 3 in the Phase 1 serial spine (001→002→003); task 002 (the 13-file Kanban hoist) depends on this boundary being clean before it adds new `@spaarke/ui-components` imports for the hoisted components. PR #508 itself is closed as superseded at project wrap-up (task 090), not by this task.</notes>

